{"units":[
{"id":"pkg/router/breaker_test.go:TestReconcileUnchangedKeyPreservesBreakerState","summary":"Test constructs a two-step breaker instead of the one-step breaker so it matches the new groupBreaker type. Test-only type swap; same settings.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"Test now builds a two-step breaker","confidence":0.9,"reason":"Test-only constructor swap to match the new breaker type, with unchanged settings and assertions.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"pkg/router/breaker_test.go:TestReconcileChangedKeyResetsBreaker","summary":"Test constructs a two-step breaker instead of the one-step breaker so it matches the new groupBreaker type. Test-only type swap; same settings.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"Test now builds a two-step breaker","confidence":0.9,"reason":"Test-only constructor swap to match the new breaker type, with unchanged settings and assertions.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"pkg/router/router.go:type handlerEntry","summary":"handlerEntry now holds the two-step groupBreaker and a per-handler watches context with its cancel func. Reconcile uses the cancel to end watches when the handler is replaced or removed.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"handlerEntry gains per-handler watch context and two-step breaker","confidence":0.8,"reason":"Adds fields that carry lifecycle and cancellation state for long-lived watches, and changes the breaker type.","risk_signals":["struct fields added","concurrency","resource lifecycle"],"focus":["every handlerEntry construction site goes through newHandlerEntry so endWatches is never nil","the breaker type change is compatible with all users"]},
{"id":"pkg/router/router.go:newHandlerEntry","summary":"New constructor builds a handlerEntry with a fresh breaker and a cancelable watches context. Reconcile now uses it for both new and changed groups.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"New constructor creates entry with cancelable watch context","confidence":0.8,"reason":"Creates a context per handler whose cancellation controls watch lifetime, so a leak or missed cancel changes runtime behavior.","risk_signals":["concurrency","resource lifecycle"],"focus":["the cancel func is always called when the entry is retired, or the context leaks","the context is rooted at Background, not the reconcile ctx"]},
{"id":"pkg/router/router.go:type servingEntry","summary":"servingEntry now carries the groupBreaker type and the handler's watches context, so the serving path can scope watches to the handler.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"servingEntry carries watch context and new breaker type","confidence":0.75,"reason":"Adds a field the request path uses to end watches, and changes the breaker type used on every request.","risk_signals":["struct fields added","concurrency"],"focus":["watches is set for every servingEntry that serves requests","the snapshot copy holds a context that outlives the entry only until cancel"]},
{"id":"pkg/router/router.go:NewGrafanaRouter","summary":"Router creates a router-wide cancelable watches context at construction. closeWatches uses it to end all watches at shutdown.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Router creates a router-wide watch context","confidence":0.75,"reason":"Introduces the shutdown-level cancellation that terminates every in-flight watch.","risk_signals":["concurrency","shutdown behavior"],"focus":["endWatches is called on every shutdown path","test routers built without NewGrafanaRouter leave watches nil"]},
{"id":"pkg/router/router.go:(*GrafanaRouter).reconcile","summary":"A changed key now replaces the handlerEntry with a new one instead of mutating it in place. Replaced and removed entries are collected and their watches ended after publish, so clients re-watch the new backend.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Reconcile replaces changed entries and ends their watches after publish","confidence":0.88,"reason":"Changes how handler swaps happen and terminates long-lived client streams on backend change or removal.","risk_signals":["concurrency","connection lifecycle","behavior change for streaming clients"],"focus":["ending watches happens after publish and outside any lock the watch handlers take","an unchanged key still keeps the same entry and its watches","early error or continue paths do not skip retiring entries"]},
{"id":"pkg/router/router.go:(*GrafanaRouter).publish","summary":"publish copies each entry's watches context into the servingEntry snapshot so request handling can bind watches to the current handler.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Snapshot now carries each entry's watch context","confidence":0.75,"reason":"Wires the watch lifetime into the snapshot read on every request.","risk_signals":["concurrency","snapshot contents changed"],"focus":["entries built by tests or other paths with nil watches are handled by serveWatch"]}
]}

{"units":[
{"id":"pkg/router/aggregate_discovery.go:newDiscoveredAggregateBackend","summary":"The aggregate backend's ReverseProxy now sets FlushInterval to -1, so each write is flushed to the client at once. Responses that carry a Content-Length used to be buffered, and now they are flushed per write.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Aggregate discovery proxy now flushes after every write","confidence":0.7,"reason":"Changes ReverseProxy buffering and flushing for every response through this backend, which affects streaming and throughput.","risk_signals":["streaming/flush behavior changed"],"focus":["Large non-watch responses with Content-Length are now flushed per write, so check the throughput cost"]},
{"id":"pkg/router/forward.go:NewForwardBackend","summary":"The forward backend's ReverseProxy now sets FlushInterval to -1, so each write is flushed to the client at once. Watch events no longer depend on the response lacking a Content-Length.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Forward backend proxy now flushes after every write","confidence":0.7,"reason":"Changes ReverseProxy buffering and flushing for all forwarded traffic, which affects streaming and throughput.","risk_signals":["streaming/flush behavior changed"],"focus":["Per-write flushing cost for large List responses through forward backends"]},
{"id":"pkg/router/proxy_errors.go:const streamingFlushInterval","summary":"Adds a constant, -1, which tells ReverseProxy to flush after every write. The proxies elsewhere in this PR use it. The constant itself changes nothing at runtime.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"New streamingFlushInterval constant set to -1","confidence":0.8,"reason":"A new constant with no behavior of its own. The behavior change is in the proxies that use it.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"pkg/router/st_fallback.go:type singleTenantFallback","summary":"The breakers cache now stores the groupBreaker alias, which is the two-step breaker, instead of the one-step CircuitBreaker. This is a type change that follows the breaker.go change.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"refactor","headline":"ST fallback breaker cache uses the two-step groupBreaker type","confidence":0.75,"reason":"A type substitution that follows the breaker change. The behavior lives in breaker.go.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"pkg/router/st_fallback.go:newSingleTenantFallback","summary":"The LRU for breakers is now constructed with the groupBreaker type. Only the type parameter changes.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"refactor","headline":"Breaker LRU constructed with groupBreaker type","confidence":0.8,"reason":"Only the type parameter changes, to match the struct field.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"pkg/router/st_fallback.go:(*singleTenantFallback).forward","summary":"The single-tenant fallback proxy now sets FlushInterval to -1, so each write is flushed to the client at once. Watch streaming no longer depends on the Content-Length heuristic.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"ST fallback proxy now flushes after every write","confidence":0.7,"reason":"Changes ReverseProxy flushing for all single-tenant fallback traffic, which affects streaming and throughput.","risk_signals":["streaming/flush behavior changed"],"focus":["Check that the new flushing interacts correctly with ModifyResponse and checkStackOrigin"]},
{"id":"pkg/router/st_fallback.go:(*singleTenantFallback).breakerForDestination","summary":"The return type changes to the groupBreaker alias. The key and lookup logic are unchanged, and callers must now use the two-step Allow API.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"refactor","headline":"breakerForDestination returns the two-step groupBreaker type","confidence":0.7,"reason":"A signature type change that follows the breaker change. The key and cache logic are untouched.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]}
]}

{"units":[
{"id":"pkg/router/breaker.go:type statusRecorder","summary":"statusRecorder gains an optional onStatus callback invoked when the final status is written. It is the hook that lets the breaker learn the outcome before the body finishes.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"statusRecorder gets onStatus callback for status-time reporting","confidence":0.7,"reason":"Adds a struct field that drives breaker accounting timing for every proxied request.","risk_signals":["struct field added","breaker accounting timing"],"focus":["onStatus is only set in serveThroughBreaker; other users of statusRecorder see nil and are unaffected"]},
{"id":"pkg/router/breaker.go:(*statusRecorder).WriteHeader","summary":"WriteHeader now calls onStatus with the final status (>=200 or 101) before forwarding the header. The callback runs synchronously inside the response write path.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"WriteHeader now reports final status to breaker callback","confidence":0.8,"reason":"Changes when circuit-breaker outcomes are recorded, on the hot response path.","risk_signals":["concurrency","breaker accounting timing","callback in write path"],"focus":["callback runs before the header reaches the client; confirm it cannot block or panic","1xx informational codes other than 101 correctly do not report","repeated WriteHeader calls only report once via sync.Once"]},
{"id":"pkg/router/breaker.go:type groupBreaker","summary":"Introduces groupBreaker as an alias for gobreaker's two-step circuit breaker so outcomes can be reported separately from the call.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"refactor","headline":"Add groupBreaker alias for the two-step circuit breaker","confidence":0.75,"reason":"A type alias only; the behavioral change is in newGroupBreaker and serveThroughBreaker.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"pkg/router/breaker.go:newGroupBreaker","summary":"newGroupBreaker now constructs a TwoStepCircuitBreaker with the same settings. This changes the API callers use to record outcomes.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"newGroupBreaker builds a two-step breaker instead of a one-shot","confidence":0.8,"reason":"Changes the breaker implementation used for all groups; semantics depend on callers reporting every outcome.","risk_signals":["breaker semantics changed"],"focus":["every Allow() caller must call done exactly once, or the half-open slot leaks","the same Settings (IsExcluded, ReadyToTrip) still apply under two-step"]},
{"id":"pkg/router/breaker.go:serveThroughBreaker","summary":"The request is no longer run inside cb.Execute. It uses Allow() and reports the outcome when the response status is written, or on return or panic, guarded by sync.Once. This stops a long watch from holding a half-open breaker's trial slot.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Breaker outcome reported at status write, not handler return","confidence":0.9,"reason":"Rewrites breaker accounting, panic handling and ordering of the open-state 503 path.","risk_signals":["concurrency","panic handling","error handling changed","breaker accounting timing"],"focus":["a handler that writes the body without calling WriteHeader is still reported on return","the panic path reports once and re-panics, including http.ErrAbortHandler","status 5xx at header time is counted as a failure, and caller-gone is still excluded","Execute used to recover and re-panic; confirm equivalent state handling"]},
{"id":"pkg/router/breaker_test.go:withGroupHandlerAndBreaker","summary":"Test helper parameter type changed to the groupBreaker alias to match production.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"Test helper takes groupBreaker type","confidence":0.9,"reason":"Test-only type signature update to match the new breaker type.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"pkg/router/breaker_test.go:TestHandleFuncBreakerHalfOpenCapRejectsConcurrentTrial","summary":"Test now builds a two-step breaker so it matches the production type. The assertions are unchanged.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"Half-open cap test uses two-step breaker","confidence":0.9,"reason":"Test-only constructor swap, with no assertions removed or changed.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"pkg/router/breaker_test.go:tripBreaker","summary":"Test helper trips the breaker through Allow() and done(err) instead of Execute. This is the equivalent forced failure for a two-step breaker.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"tripBreaker uses Allow/done to force a failure","confidence":0.88,"reason":"Test-only helper adapted to the new breaker API with equivalent effect.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]}
]}
